-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_err_cppstart_space.pcpp - Lexical: a cppstart block ending in a blank splice

  Break step of lex_splices: a cppstart block's last line of C++ ending
  in a splice with a blank after its backslash warns, LX0201 at the
  backslash, and is still a splice that would join cppend into the C++,
  LX0014 at the same backslash. The marked line ends in the splice, so
  its marker is a block-comment marker.
  Its bytes are part of the test (see above): edit it with an editor
  that keeps them as they are.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_cppstart_space;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

cppstart source
int GX = 1; /* // WARN LX0201@60 // ERROR LX0014@59 // */ \ 
cppend;

begin
  println("{}", 1);
end.
